# Sources:
#   https://microsoft.github.io/language-server-protocol/specifications/lsp/3.17/specification/
#   docs/DIALECT.md (§4.21: what tools read of Ljós's syntax; §5.1: ts-lts-syntax)
# `ljos lsp` is Ljós's own: Qt has nothing to compare it with.
# A file given here is written without the spaces its doc string is indented by, so the
# first column of a line is 1. A finding is said as `ljos check` says it, at the line and
# column the editor shows: the protocol's own count from 0, plus one.

@ljos-only @headless
Feature: An editor reads Ljós through `ljos lsp`
  `ljos lsp` speaks the language server protocol over its standard input
  and output. An editor that opens a QML file, a `.ts` module or an
  `.lts` module is told what `ljos check` finds in it, at the place in
  the text it shows, and told again as the text changes. Where the
  finding is a `.ts` module that uses Ljós's syntax, the editor is
  offered the rename to `.lts`. A saved `.lts` module's declaration is
  written again. Between messages the server waits; it looks at nothing.

  Scenario: An opened QML file is told what the check finds in it
    Given the file "Pad.qml":
      """qml
      import Ljos.Ui
      Item {
          property real gap: 4
          function grow() { gap = "8" }
      }
      """
    When the language server opens "Pad.qml"
    Then the language server publishes for "Pad.qml":
      """
      4:29: error: `gap` is a real; this gives it a string [ts-assign-type]
      """

  Scenario: A `.ts` module's Ljós syntax is reported where it is, with its rename offered
    Given the file "size.ts":
      """ts
      export function margin(big: boolean): number {
        return match (big) {
          when true: 12;
          when false: 4;
        }
      }
      """
    When the language server is asked for the actions on "size.ts"
    Then the language server publishes for "size.ts":
      """
      2:10: error: `match` is Ljós syntax, which stock TypeScript tools cannot read in a `.ts` file; rename `size.ts` to `size.lts` [ts-lts-syntax]
      """
    And the language server offers the action "Rename size.ts to size.lts"
    And the action "Rename size.ts to size.lts" renames "size.ts" to "size.lts"

  Scenario: An `.lts` module's finding after a `match` is where it is
    Given the file "width.lts":
      """ts
      export function width(thick: boolean): number {
        return match (thick) {
          when true: 3;
          when false: 1;
        }
      }
      export const gap = [1].length
      """
    When the language server opens "width.lts"
    Then the language server publishes for "width.lts":
      """
      7:14: error: `gap` is exported from an `.lts` module, so its value needs a declared type for the module's declaration [lts-export-type]
      """

  Scenario: A change is checked as the editor has it, not as it is on disk
    Given the file "width.lts":
      """ts
      export const gap = [1].length
      """
    When the language server opens "width.lts" and it is changed to:
      """ts
      export const gap: number = [1].length
      """
    Then the language server publishes nothing for "width.lts"

  Scenario: Saving an `.lts` module writes its declaration
    Given the file "width.lts":
      """ts
      export const gap: number = 4
      """
    And the file "tsconfig.json":
      """json
      { "extends": "./.ljos/tsconfig.base.json" }
      """
    When the language server opens "width.lts" and saves it
    Then the language server publishes nothing for "width.lts"
    And the file ".ljos/types/width.d.lts.ts" is:
      """ts
      // Generated by ljos check from width.lts; do not edit.
      export declare const gap: number;
      """

  Scenario: The rename edits an importer the editor has open as the editor has it, unsaved
    Given the file "size.ts":
      """ts
      export function margin(big: boolean): number {
        return match (big) {
          when true: 12;
          when false: 4;
        }
      }
      """
    And the file "Pad.qml":
      """qml
      import Ljos.Ui
      import "size.ts" as Size
      Item {
          property real gap: Size.margin(true)
      }
      """
    And the editor has "Pad.qml" open, changed to:
      """qml
      import Ljos.Ui
      import "size.ts" as Size
      Item {
          property real gap: Size.margin(true)
          property real inset: Size.margin(false)
      }
      """
    When the language server is asked for the actions on "size.ts"
    Then the action "Rename size.ts to size.lts" leaves "Pad.qml" in the editor as:
      """qml
      import Ljos.Ui
      import "size.lts" as Size
      Item {
          property real gap: Size.margin(true)
          property real inset: Size.margin(false)
      }
      """

  Scenario: A file is checked with the other files the editor has open as it has them
    Given the file "width.lts":
      """ts
      export const gap: number = 4
      """
    And the file "line.ts":
      """ts
      import { gap } from "./width.lts"
      export const wide: number = gap
      """
    And the file "tsconfig.json":
      """json
      { "extends": "./.ljos/tsconfig.base.json" }
      """
    And the editor has "width.lts" open, changed to:
      """ts
      export const gap: string = "4"
      """
    When the language server opens "line.ts"
    Then the language server publishes for "line.ts":
      """
      2:29: error: `wide` is a number; this gives it a string [ts-assign-type]
      """

  Scenario: Saving a module checks again the open files that import it
    Given the file "width.lts":
      """ts
      export const gap: number = 4
      """
    And the file "line.ts":
      """ts
      import { gap } from "./width.lts"
      export const wide: number = gap
      """
    And the file "tsconfig.json":
      """json
      { "extends": "./.ljos/tsconfig.base.json" }
      """
    And the editor has "line.ts" open
    When the language server opens "width.lts", it is changed to this and saved:
      """ts
      export const gap: string = "4"
      """
    Then the language server publishes nothing for "width.lts"
    And the language server publishes for "line.ts":
      """
      2:29: error: `wide` is a number; this gives it a string [ts-assign-type]
      """

  Scenario: Closing a module unsaved checks again the open files that import it
    Given the file "width.lts":
      """ts
      export const gap: number = 4
      """
    And the file "line.ts":
      """ts
      import { gap } from "./width.lts"
      export const wide: number = gap
      """
    And the file "tsconfig.json":
      """json
      { "extends": "./.ljos/tsconfig.base.json" }
      """
    And the editor has "width.lts" open, changed to:
      """ts
      export const gap: string = "4"
      """
    When the language server opens "line.ts", then "width.lts" is closed
    Then the language server publishes nothing for "line.ts"
